 ## Pits AI without an API bill
 
-`/#ai` stores the caller's message. The owner’s Site-created PAX PITS plugin supplies `open_pax_pits` and `reply_pax_pits` to ChatGPT. ChatGPT generates the actual reply and writes it back to the same authenticated user. No timer, background agent or canned reply is represented as an AI reply. No external API is called. A pending message does not receive an automatic in-site response just by opening the app. Personal plugin distribution to other users is unverified. Existing Pits Capsule is linked as a separate AI companion; it does not share history.
+`/#ai` now runs an on-device language model in a dedicated Web Worker. After initial model preparation, sending a message immediately generates and streams a reply inside the same page and saves it to the caller's private history. Users can stop generation and retry; a save retry reuses the already generated text. A cancelled/deleted prompt cannot be resurrected by a late reply. No external paid inference API or new credential is used.
 
+Two pinned public Qwen models are available: standard Qwen3-1.7B (about 1.5 GB download, WebGPU with shader-f16 required) and light Qwen3-0.6B (about 610–650 MB including runtime/tokenizer, WebGPU q4f16 or WASM q8). Actual transfer/cache requirements can vary. Light is preselected on browsers without navigator.gpu. Other unsupported GPU configurations receive an explicit instruction to choose light; the app does not silently download a second model. Model files come from Hugging Face and its delivery hosts, the pinned Transformers.js runtime is served by the Site, and the matching WASM runtime loads from jsDelivr. Only model files/normal HTTP connection metadata go to those distribution sites; chat text is used locally and stored through the authenticated Site API.
+
+The lightweight model is materially less capable than ChatGPT. Japanese phrasing, persona consistency, and factual quality can be poor. Never describe this as ChatGPT-equivalent or as certified safe advice. Preparation is user initiated and states the download size and data-charge implications. It can fail on low-memory devices, old browsers, or blocked networks; no paid or hosted inference fallback is silently enabled.
+
+The existing Site-created MCP plugin is retained for optional ChatGPT use and historical compatibility, but the in-app AI screen does not require opening ChatGPT or invoking a plugin.
 Per-user limits: 20 AI submissions/day, 5 unanswered submissions, 30 saved replies/day. Existing image API endpoint now rejects before any provider request, even if a key exists. Existing secret keys are not changed.
 
 ## Backups and recovery
